{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdLociDensity","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.faddeevPhi_uniqueUpToScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.faddeevPhi_uniqueUpToScalar","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.lean#L74-L84","doc":"**Uniqueness conditional on class axioms.** Any `FaddeevPhiPhysical` solution\nis proportional to `phiBProd`. The conclusion is conditional on the class fields\n(shift equations + strip-growth + NF); no further hypotheses appear as explicit\narguments. Composes the full sorry-free chain:\n`PhiBProdLociDensity.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_normalForm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.hNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.hNF","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.lean#L72-L72","doc":"`Φ` is in meromorphic normal form on `ℂ` (Lean regularity, not a math\nhypothesis — any meromorphic function can be represented this way). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.instStripGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.instStripGrowth","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.lean#L69-L69","doc":"`Φ` is comparable in modulus to `phiBProd` (physical strip-growth bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.toFaddeevPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical.toFaddeevPhi","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.lean#L66-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.FaddeevPhiPhysical","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiFullUniqueness.lean#L53-L72","doc":"**`Φ_b` with strip-growth + normal form (conjecture-class, §3b).**\nExtends `FaddeevPhi` with the two regularity conditions that the uniqueness\nchain needs. Both are **carried axioms** (open inputs packaged as class fields):\n\n- **strip-growth comparability** to `phiBProd` — the physical asymptotic\n  condition (Faddeev–Kashaev) excluding elliptic multipliers.\n- **meromorphic normal form** on `ℂ` — a Lean technicality (total-function\n  values at poles are 0); holds by construction for quotients of entire\n  functions.\n\nThe class is non-vacuous: `phiBProd` itself satisfies all fields. But\ninstantiating it for a *second* solution IS the remaining analytic content\n(the open input that the shift equations alone do not provide). ","signatureChunk":0}]}